<section className="section problem-section"><div className="wrap problem-layout"><div className="intro reveal"><p className="eyebrow">The real problem</p><h2>More budget won't fix <span className="gradient-text">a leaky funnel.</span></h2><p className="lead">When campaigns look active but growth stalls, the answer isn't always to spend more. It starts with understanding where the journey breaks down.</p><a className="btn" href="#contact">Request a Free Ads Review <span className="arrow">↗</span></a></div><div className="problem-list"><article className="problem reveal"><span className="problem-no">01 /</span><div><h3>Clicks, but not enough customers</h3><p>Campaigns attract attention, but landing pages, offer clarity or audience intent may be preventing action.</p></div></article><article className="problem reveal reveal-delay-1"><span className="problem-no">02 /</span><div><h3>Leads that don't turn into revenue</h3><p>Lead volume alone can hide poor fit. We focus on the path from targeting and enquiry through to meaningful business outcomes.</p></div></article><article className="problem reveal reveal-delay-2"><span className="problem-no">03 /</span><div><h3>Tracking you can't fully trust</h3><p>Incomplete conversion signals make it difficult to know which campaigns deserve more investment.</p></div></article><article className="problem reveal reveal-delay-3"><span className="problem-no">04 /</span><div><h3>Reporting without clear next steps</h3><p>You should understand what changed, why it matters and what the team plans to test next.</p></div></article></div></div></section>






